      "message": "feat(ui): load machine and post files from the user's disk in the browser\n\nThe browser build reads a .mch or .cps file as bytes from the picker,\na folder picker (webkitdirectory) or a drop. A session store in app\nkeeps each file that passes the disk checks, by its file name. The\nexisting readers consult it first, so LoadMachineFile, SelectPostFile\nand the MCP tools run unchanged and stay undoable. Load machine and\nLoad post are live in the browser; the Machine page adds Load folder.\nSeveral dropped files join the machine and post lists, and each bad\nfile is refused by name on one status line. A saved project that names\na file which is not loaded again is refused by that name.\n\nFixes #2950\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
